# Code owners for tracebloc/.github
#
# This repository is the org's enforcement root: 96 caller workflows across 14
# repos reference `tracebloc/.github/.github/workflows/*.yml@main`, and every
# one of them passes `secrets: inherit`. A change merged here takes effect in
# every repo on the next workflow run, and reaches every secret those repos
# hold.
#
# Branch protection on `main` already sets `require_code_owner_reviews: true`,
# but no CODEOWNERS file existed — so the requirement was vacuous and any two
# of the seven org members could land a change to the gates themselves. This
# file makes that flag mean something.
#
# Note on self-merge: as sole code owner, @LukasWodka cannot approve his own
# PRs, so his changes still rely on the admin bypass (`enforce_admins: false`).
# That is deliberate for now — the control this file adds is over the other six
# members' changes. Adding a second owner would make it a true two-person rule
# at the cost of a second gatekeeper.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @LukasWodka

# The reusable workflows that define every gate in the org.
/.github/workflows/         @LukasWodka

# Scripts invoked by those workflows.
/scripts/                   @LukasWodka
